{"paper": "CHSL-Tier1-04-Jul-2024-Shift3.pdf", "status": "ok", "mode": "sequential", "splitter": "qdot", "section_slice": true, "extracted_count": 25, "tagged_count": 25, "questions": [{"n": 1, "text": "", "options": [{"text": "3", "added": false}, {"text": "5", "added": false}, {"text": "4", "added": false}, {"text": "2", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": true, "topic": "Simplification", "sub": "other", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 2, "text": "", "options": [{"text": "11", "added": false}, {"text": "22", "added": false}, {"text": "10", "added": false}, {"text": "20", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": true, "topic": "Simplification", "sub": "other", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 3, "text": "Express the following as decimals, respectively. 20%,0.5%,0.03%", "options": [{"text": "0.02,0.005,0.0003", "added": false}, {"text": "0.02,0.005,0.003", "added": false}, {"text": "0.2,0.005,0.0003", "added": false}, {"text": "0.2,0.0005,0.0003", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Percentage", "sub": "increase-decrease", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 4, "text": "The diameter of a cylinder is 14 cm and its height is 9 cm. Find the total surface area of the cylinder.", "options": [], "options_source": "missing", "image_only": false, "topic": "Mensuration 3D", "sub": "cylinder", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 5, "text": "", "options": [{"text": "4", "added": false}, {"text": "3", "added": false}, {"text": "1", "added": false}, {"text": "2", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": true, "topic": "Simplification", "sub": "other", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 6, "text": "A car covers a certain distance in 85 minutes, if it runs at a speed of 36 km/hr. The speed at which the car must run to reduce the time of journey to 51 minutes will be:", "options": [{"text": "70 km/hr", "added": false}, {"text": "80 km/hr", "added": false}, {"text": "60 km/hr", "added": false}, {"text": "50 km/hr", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Time-Speed-Distance", "sub": "basic-tsd", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 7, "text": "", "options": [{"text": "₹ 1400 crore", "added": false}, {"text": "₹ 1325 crore", "added": false}, {"text": "₹ 1350 crore", "added": false}, {"text": "₹ 1225 crore", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": true, "topic": "Simplification", "sub": "other", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 8, "text": "Two circles with centres M and N have radii 5 cm and 8 cm, respectively. The circles touch each other externally at point T. A line PR is drawn such that the points M, T and N lie on PR, P being closer to M. From P, a tangent PQ = 12 cm is drawn to the circle with centre M touching at Q, and from R, another tangent RS = 15 cm is drawn to the circle with centre N touching at S. What is the length (in cm) of PR?", "options": [{"text": "37", "added": false}, {"text": "43", "added": false}, {"text": "53", "added": false}, {"text": "26", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Circles-Polygons", "sub": "tangents-and-chords", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 9, "text": "", "options": [{"text": "5", "added": false}, {"text": "6", "added": false}, {"text": "−5", "added": false}, {"text": "−6", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": true, "topic": "Simplification", "sub": "other", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 10, "text": "Find the third proportion to 36 and 48.", "options": [{"text": "36", "added": false}, {"text": "54", "added": false}, {"text": "64", "added": false}, {"text": "48", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Ratio-Proportion", "sub": "proportion", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 11, "text": "", "options": [], "options_source": "missing", "image_only": true, "topic": "Simplification", "sub": "other", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 12, "text": "", "options": [], "options_source": "missing", "image_only": true, "topic": "Simplification", "sub": "other", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 13, "text": "The total surface area of a solid hemisphere of diameter 28 cm is:", "options": [{"text": "1784 cm2", "added": false}, {"text": "1488 cm2", "added": false}, {"text": "1648 cm2", "added": false}, {"text": "1848 cm2", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Mensuration 3D", "sub": "sphere-hemisphere", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 14, "text": "", "options": [{"text": "24", "added": false}, {"text": "20", "added": false}, {"text": "22", "added": false}, {"text": "25", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": true, "topic": "Simplification", "sub": "other", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 15, "text": "∆DEF and ∆GHI are two similar triangles. If DE = 64 cm, GH = 24 cm and the perimeter of ∆GHI is 72 cm, then what is the sum of the lengths (in cm) of the sides EF and FD of the ∆DEF?", "options": [{"text": "192", "added": false}, {"text": "96", "added": false}, {"text": "128", "added": false}, {"text": "82", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Geometry", "sub": "congruence-and-similarity", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 16, "text": "", "options": [], "options_source": "missing", "image_only": true, "topic": "Simplification", "sub": "other", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 17, "text": "", "options": [], "options_source": "missing", "image_only": true, "topic": "Simplification", "sub": "other", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 18, "text": "The price of pulses has increased by 45%. By what percentage (rounded off to the nearest integer) the increased price of the pulses should be reduced so that the price of the pulses remains unaltered?", "options": [{"text": "45", "added": false}, {"text": "31", "added": false}, {"text": "41", "added": false}, {"text": "35", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Percentage", "sub": "increase-decrease", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 19, "text": "To finish a work in 12 days, 8 workers are engaged. After 2 days, due to some urgency, the work is to be finished in next 2 days. How many more workers are to be engaged now to finish it on time?", "options": [{"text": "30", "added": false}, {"text": "32", "added": false}, {"text": "36", "added": false}, {"text": "40", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Time-Work", "sub": "efficiency", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 20, "text": "Study the given graph and answer the question that follows. Ratio of imports to exports from two companies over the years. In how many of the given years were the imports more than the exports of Company N ?", "options": [{"text": "2", "added": false}, {"text": "1", "added": false}, {"text": "3", "added": false}, {"text": "4", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Data Interpretation", "sub": "mixed-graphs", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 21, "text": "", "options": [], "options_source": "missing", "image_only": true, "topic": "Simplification", "sub": "other", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 22, "text": "A circle of diameter 26 cm has two equal chords of length 10 cm each, separated by a distance h cm. What is the value of h?", "options": [{"text": "18", "added": false}, {"text": "12", "added": false}, {"text": "24", "added": false}, {"text": "16", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Circles-Polygons", "sub": "tangents-and-chords", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 23, "text": "The age of a father will be double the age of his son ten years later. 10 years ago, the father’s age was six times the age of the son. How many years from now, the ratio of their ages will be 3 : 2?", "options": [{"text": "35", "added": false}, {"text": "30", "added": false}, {"text": "20", "added": false}, {"text": "25", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Ages", "sub": "ratio-of-ages", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 24, "text": "The given line graph shows the number of scooters manufactured (in thousands) by companies X and Z, over the years. In which of the following years was the difference between the production by companies X and Z the maximum among the given years?", "options": [{"text": "2018", "added": false}, {"text": "2017", "added": false}, {"text": "2020", "added": false}, {"text": "2019", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Data Interpretation", "sub": "line-graph", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 25, "text": "Rahna decided to buy a scooty that costs ₹40,000. The shopkeeper agreed to sell the scooty under the condition of ₹25,000 cash down payment of ₹4,000 each month for four months. Find the rate of interest at which the shopkeeper sold the scooty under the instalment scheme.", "options": [], "options_source": "missing", "image_only": false, "topic": "Simple Interest", "sub": "si-instalments", "key_answer": null}]}